<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ion Antonescu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1882">1882</a>–<a href="/years/1946">1946</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ion Antonescu was a Romanian army officer who ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a> as Conducător from 1940 to 1944. Appointed prime minister by Carol II in 1940, he forced the king's abdication, crushed the Iron Guard in 1941 and took Romania into the war against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> as an ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, while his regime deported and killed hundreds of thousands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romani-people">Roma</a>. He was arrested in King Michael's coup of August 1944 and executed in 1946.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ion-antonescu.jpg" alt="Ion Antonescu" width="320" height="454" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ion_Antonescu_1941.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In Romania the Iron Guard came to power with General <b>Ion Antonescu</b> in 1940, the only fascist movement outside Germany and Italy to do so without foreign help, and was repressed the next year.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/fascism">Fascism · Spread &amp; Variants</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Ion Antonescu</b> led it into war as an Axis ally until King Michael's coup of August 1944.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-romania">Kingdom of Romania</a></li></ul></section>
